  "date": "October 2026",
  "abstract": "Covers the Agent Client Protocol (ACP), the JSON-RPC 2.0 protocol between code editors or other UIs (Clients) and AI coding agents (Agents). ACP v1 (protocolVersion 1, schema v1.24.1) is the current line: initialization and version negotiation, capabilities, authentication, session setup, load, resume, list and close, prompt turns and stop reasons, session/update variants, tool calls and permission requests, fs and terminal Client methods, cancellation, error codes, _meta and underscore extensions, absolute paths and 1-based lines, and stdio framing. The ACP v2 draft (schema v2.0.0-alpha.7) is a preview with posture build, to be implemented only behind version negotiation and a feature flag beside v1, with a per-role migration checklist. SKILL.md holds the invariants and workflow; references split out the version lines and upgrade, the v1 lifecycle, tool calls and Client methods, and the v2 draft surface.",
